  "narration": [
    {
      "t": 0.5,
      "text": "A drop in the zep ledger is not finished just because you closed it. Let me show you."
    },
    {
      "t": 6.15,
      "text": "We open a drop to work in, and zep hands us a nonce for it. Keep that in mind, it matters at the end."
    },
    {
      "t": 13.41,
      "text": "Stage a fact into the drop. Nothing surprising here."
    },
    {
      "t": 17.47,
      "text": "Now watch what happens if we just close it."
    },
    {
      "t": 22.8,
      "text": "It says it closed, but look at the state line, and look at the anchor. That is not a finished drop."
    },
    {
      "t": 29.52,
      "text": "The nonce is still sitting on disk next to the drop, and zep will print it again for us."
    },
    {
      "t": 35.38,
      "text": "So we close it again, this time passing that nonce along with it."
    },
    {
      "t": 40.8,
      "text": "Now it is sealed and it has an anchor of its own."
    },
    {
      "t": 44.5,
      "text": "Sealed, with a real anchor. That is the difference, and it is easy to miss."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Teaches that closing a drop without its nonce leaves a provisional record, and where the nonce can be read back from."
}
